From: Ventuno integration <ventuno@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] platforms: preserve readiness received before the start callback

The signal socket may deliver READY before the LXC PID pipe is dispatched.
Only advance STARTING to STARTED in the pipe callback: retain READY and do
not resurrect a platform already being stopped. PID and console setup must
still run. Reject readiness outside the running startup lifecycle.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/platforms.c b/platforms.c
--- a/platforms.c
+++ b/platforms.c
@@ -1139,7 +1139,11 @@ static void _read_platform_pipefd_cb(int fd, short event, void *arg)
 
 	pv_log(DEBUG, "started platform '%s' with pid %d", p->name,
 	       p->init_pid);
-	pv_platform_set_status(p, PLAT_STARTED);
+	/* READY can arrive on the control socket before this PID notification.
+	 * Complete startup bookkeeping without regressing readiness or a stop.
+	 */
+	if (p->status.current == PLAT_STARTING)
+		pv_platform_set_status(p, PLAT_STARTED);
 }
 
 int pv_platform_start(struct pv_platform *p)
@@ -1488,6 +1492,11 @@ int pv_platform_set_ready(struct pv_platform *p)
 	if (p->status.goal != PLAT_READY)
 		return -1;
 
+	if (p->status.current != PLAT_STARTING &&
+	    p->status.current != PLAT_STARTED &&
+	    p->status.current != PLAT_READY)
+		return -1;
+
 	pv_platform_set_status(p, PLAT_READY);
 	return 0;
 }
